{#- The repair ladder's regeneration of one beat (FR-REPAIR-1,2, docs/02 §5's Regeneration row;
#151).

Edit in place: the ``system`` block holds the generation inputs of the render the beat came
from (the rating guidance always first, FR-RATE-4; the custom instructions; a scenario story's
scenario text; the rendering character's definition, or for a narrator beat the director's
notes; the pinned memories; the scene, the working memory, the retrieved context and the
canon it may know, and ``## Tracked values``, #187), then ``## Repair``: the beat as it was rendered, the canon facts it
contradicted, the facts that hang on them (their neighborhood) and one line per constraint the
rewrite must keep. The ``user`` block is the player input. The rewritten beat comes back as the
call's ``response_schema`` (one beat of the same kind: its text and the propositions it
declares). -#}
{% block system %}
{% if rating_guidance %}
## Content rating guidance
{{ rating_guidance }}

{% endif %}
{% if custom_instructions %}
## Custom instructions
{{ custom_instructions }}

{% endif %}
{% if scenario_text %}
{{ scenario_text }}

{% endif %}
{% for character in character_definitions %}
## You are {{ character.name }}
{{ character.definition }}
{% if character.deflection_style %}
When {{ character.name }} refuses or changes the subject: {{ character.deflection_style }}
{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% if director_notes %}
## Director guidance (not facts)
{{ director_notes }}

{% endif %}
{% if pinned_memories %}
## Pinned memories
{% for memory in pinned_memories %}
- {{ memory }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if summary_segments %}
## Earlier in the story
{% for segment in summary_segments %}
{{ segment }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if scene %}
## Scene
{{ scene }}

{% endif %}
{% if working_memory %}
## What you remember
{% for beat in working_memory %}
- {{ beat }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if retrieved_memories %}
## Retrieved
{% for item in retrieved_memories %}
- {{ item }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if canon_facts %}
## Canon
{% for fact in canon_facts %}
- {{ fact }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if tracked_values %}
## Tracked values
{% for line in tracked_values %}
- {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{{ tracked_syntax }}

{% endif %}
## Repair
This `{{ beat_kind }}` beat{% if voiced_characters %} of {{ voiced_characters | join(", ") }}{% endif %} broke the story's facts:
{{ rejected_text }}
{% if contradicted_facts %}

It contradicted:
{% for fact in contradicted_facts %}
- {{ fact }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if neighborhood %}

These facts hang together with them and must stay true:
{% for fact in neighborhood %}
- {{ fact }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

Rewrite only this beat, as a `{{ beat_kind }}` beat in the same voice, so that it keeps every constraint below and asserts nothing the facts above deny. Declare each factual claim it makes as a proposition (subject, relation, object).
{% for constraint in constraints %}
- {{ constraint.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% for constraint in policy_constraints %}
{{ constraint }}
{% endfor %}
{% include "steering_resolution.j2" %}
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
{{ player_input.name }}:{% if player_input.say %} "{{ player_input.say }}"{% endif %}{% if player_input.do %} *{{ player_input.do }}*{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
